    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24">

                <pb facs="0142" n="16" xml:id="pg16"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A12/77: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Houghton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-11-19T10:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                                1925—10 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>338. Your No. 337, October 29. I have talked over the matter with the President
                    and have given him a memorandum.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d24-f1"/> He will take up
                    the subject in his message to Congress on December 9 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >8</hi>].<anchor n="24" xml:id="d24-f2"/> It will receive much more
                    publicity in that way than it would from a newspaper interview. If you think
                    that there is any possibility that European countries will take steps to call a
                    conference before his message, I should be glad to be advised.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
